{"strongs": "H0100", "word": "אַגְמֹן", "translit": "ag.mon", "root": "אגמן", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun [masculine]", "gloss": "rush, bulrush", "definition": "אַגְמֹן , אַגְמוֺן noun [masculine] rush, bulrush . 1. used as cord or line Job 40:26 (of twisted rushes, or spun of rush-fibre, compare Di on the passage); as fuel Job 41:12 simile of bending head Isa 58:5 . 2. metaphor of the lowly, insignif. (|| כִּפָּה ) Isa 9:13 ; Isa 19:15 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB91')\">BDB91</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H100')\">H100</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB90')\">BDB90</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB92')\">BDB92</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אַגְמֹן</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אַגְמוֺן</bdbheb> <b>noun [masculine]</b> <highlightword>rush, bulrush</highlightword>. <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> used as cord or line <ref ref=\"Job 40:26\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(18,40,26)\">Job 40:26</ref> (of twisted rushes, or spun of rush-fibre, compare <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Di')\">Di</lookup> on the passage); as fuel <ref ref=\"Job 41:12\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(18,41,12)\">Job 41:12</ref> simile of bending head <ref ref=\"Isa 58:5\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"58\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"58\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(23,58,5)\">Isa 58:5</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> metaphor of the lowly, insignif. (|| <bdbheb>כִּפָּה</bdbheb>) <ref ref=\"Isa 9:13\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(23,9,13)\">Isa 9:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 19:15\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(23,19,15)\">Isa 19:15</ref>. </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Job 40:26", "book": "JOB", "chapter": 40, "verse": 26}, {"raw": "Job 41:12", "book": "JOB", "chapter": 41, "verse": 12}, {"raw": "Isa 58:5", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 58, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "Isa 9